# ACCESS ALGERIA — REPOSITORY ARCHITECTURE

> This file maps the repository and describes its operating flows. The map
> describes where controlled knowledge and software live; the flows describe
> how research and opportunities move through the system.

## 1. Repository map

### Strategy and governance

| Area | Location | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Control | `00_MASTER_CONTROL` | Strategic foundation and scope |
| Governance | `01_GOVERNANCE_AND_VERIFICATION` | Evidence, verification, and information quality |
| Intelligence | `02_MARKET_INTELLIGENCE`, `03_BRAND_DATABASE`, `06_PARTNERSHIP_INTELLIGENCE`, `07_01REGULATORY_INTELLIGENCE` | Market, brand, partner, and regulatory research |
| Decision | `04_OPPORTUNITY_SCORING`, `05_MARKET_ENTRY` | Opportunity assessment and entry strategy |
| Case validation | `08_ASTON_MARTIN_CASE` | Flagship case application |
| AI | `09_AI_SYSTEM` | AI use and research protocols |
| Execution | `10_MONDAY_EXECUTION_SYSTEM`, `16_OPERATIONS` | Operational workflows and execution |
| Integration | `11_SYSTEM_INTEGRATION` | System connections and information flow |
| Outputs | `12_TEMPLATES_AND_OUTPUTS`, `17_CLIENT_DELIVERY_SYSTEM` | Templates and client deliverables |
| Portfolio | `13_PORTFOLIO_AND_DASHBOARD`, `19_PERFORMANCE_MANAGEMENT` | Portfolio and performance tracking |
| System map | `14_FINAL_SYSTEM_MAP` | Lifecycle and operating model |
| Repository governance | `15_REPOSITORY_GOVERNANCE` | Repository structure, audits, and change control |
| Knowledge | `18_KNOWLEDGE_MANAGEMENT` | Knowledge retention and classification |

### Software and quality checks

| Location | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `src/data` | Country reference data and external economic-data pipeline |
| `src/document` | Gazette document parsing boundary and extraction schema |
| `src/scoring` | Opportunity scoring implementations |
| `tests` | Automated tests for the Python modules |
| `.github/workflows` | Automated Python quality workflow |
| `access-algeria-website` | Separate website workspace; currently a Vite starter scaffold |

Python and quality-tool configuration is in `pyproject.toml`, `requirements.txt`,
and `requirements-dev.txt`. The isolated dependency manifests
`requirements-comtrade-mirror.txt` and `requirements-gpl-isolated.txt` keep
their respective compatibility and licensing constraints separate.

